# An ability that triggers while the turn is being ended is put on the stack in the cleanup step, where players then get
# priority (CR 724.1f, 514.3a). Ultima destroys the Llanowar Elves that Rancor enchants; Rancor, attached to nothing, is put
# into the graveyard by the state-based actions checked as the turn ends (CR 724.1c, 704.5m), and its "return it to its
# owner's hand" triggers then, during the process, so it does not cease to exist (724.1a is about abilities that
# triggered before). It waits for the cleanup step, goes on the stack there, and resolves: Rancor is back in Bot1's hand.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Rancor
Ultima
Mox Pearl
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Rancor.Cast(Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Power = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ultima.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Cleanup]
? Step = Cleanup
? Stack.Count = 1
? Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 5
[T4 Bot2.Upkeep]

[Expect]
Turn = 4
Bot1.Hand = Forest; Rancor
Bot1.Battlefield = Forest
Bot1.Graveyard = Mox Jet; Mox Pearl; Llanowar Elves; Black Lotus
Exile = Ultima
